WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Speaker 1: We have a very interesting new&nbsp;
development in the brew now. Hypothetical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:13.040
2024 Republican presidential matchup. Ron DeSantis&nbsp;
and Donald Trump are essentially even right now in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:19.200
terms of the betting odds for 2024. Now, I want&nbsp;
to remind everybody this this is not polling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:26.320
okay? This is you go to predict it, dawg, and you&nbsp;
can bet on who you believe will be the nominee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:34.080
For the last many, many months, Donald Trump has&nbsp;
been the clear. But increasingly by a smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.520
margin favorite in terms of the betting&nbsp;
odds to be the 2024 Republican nominee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.600
Over the last two days after the FBI served a&nbsp;
search warrant at Trump's home, Ron DeSantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.480
actually pulled ahead and then as of moments ago&nbsp;
in a virtual tie. Donald Trump and Ron DeSantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:01:00.160
for 2024. In terms of not who will you vote&nbsp;
for, but who will you bet on being the nominee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:08.240
right now? In order to win a dollar, you have to&nbsp;
bet $0.37 on Donald Trump being the nominee. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.520
in order to win a dollar, you have to bet $0.36&nbsp;
on DeSantis being the nominee. It is a virtual tie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:21.280
and every reason to believe that this change is&nbsp;
tied to the search warrant and the increasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.760
legal problems for Trump. Trump pleading&nbsp;
the fifth more than 400 times yesterday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.840
which I will talk about in the next segment. In&nbsp;
terms of polling, how does the polling actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:40.240
look? It still favors Trump very clearly. New&nbsp;
polls. We have a Yahoo! News poll, YouGov, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:47.920
Yahoo! News poll from late July, early August&nbsp;
that has Trump plus nine. And then before that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:58.560
at the end of July, a Harris Harvard poll that has&nbsp;
Trump plus like 30. Okay. So it is tightening. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:04.960
also Donald Trump is still clearly the favorite&nbsp;
among current Republican voters. We are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.640
to be watching these numbers very closely. I&nbsp;
don't want to spend a lot of time on it today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.200
but we are certainly going to be keeping an eye on&nbsp;
it. The numbers are tightening. And remember that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.480
DeSantis hasn't announced anything. Trump hasn't&nbsp;
either. But Trump has been all but announcing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.280
saying things like, we might have to do it again.&nbsp;
I think you're going to be very happy with what we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:30.880
decide, etc., etc. It is not clear that Trump&nbsp;
would necessarily win a contested Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:38.160
primary, which would be an extraordinary thing&nbsp;
for a one term president who lost an unprecedented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.920
situation could be facing us in 2024, but we&nbsp;
have 2022 coming up first. And so that's where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.560
our focus will be. Let me know your thoughts&nbsp;
on where you see this Republican primary going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:54.480
Find me on Twitter at David Pakman. We will talk&nbsp;
about pleading the fifth after this short break.

